{#- The heading that turns a `secrecy: secret` entry (#49) from a fact the
    model may put in anyone's mouth into one it has to handle carefully.
    Shared by the "World info" and "Recalled lore" sections so the instruction
    is worded once and drifts in one place. Takes the already-selected secret
    bodies; the caller renders nothing at all when there are none. -#}
{%- macro secret_block(bodies) -%}
Secret knowledge — true, but NOT common knowledge in the scene. Only characters who plausibly already know a fact below may act on it; everyone else speaks and behaves as though unaware, and must not reveal it, confirm it, or hint at it. Narrate what the ignorant characters actually perceive, not what you know:

{{ bodies | join("\n\n") }}
{%- endmacro -%}
